WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:05.530
So we've now learned of a child in Iowa who
has died of Corona virus complications.

00:00:05.530 --> 00:00:09.410
And this was the first death of a miner there
during the pandemic.

00:00:09.410 --> 00:00:13.410
And meanwhile, schools are opening today in
Iowa.

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:20.160
Now, there are schools in Iowa that decided
we're going to go remote for now, or at least

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:24.080
they thought they decided it because then
the governors, the governor of Iowa, came

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:27.240
in and is actually forcing some schools to
open.

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:30.140
So there's about three or four different stories
here.

00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:36.940
One is this is exactly why lots of places
try to make it illegal or at least a violation

00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:42.949
of contracts for teachers to go on strike
so that when the governor says jump, instead

00:00:42.949 --> 00:00:44.750
of saying, why are we jumping?

00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:45.780
That doesn't make sense.

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:46.989
They say, how high?

00:00:46.989 --> 00:00:49.239
And this is exactly an example of that.

00:00:49.239 --> 00:00:50.890
It relates to collective bargaining.

00:00:50.890 --> 00:00:52.030
It relates to unions.

00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:54.640
It relates to so many different things on
the labor side.

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:56.969
But it's not our focus today.

00:00:56.969 --> 00:01:02.929
The other side of it is really the craziness
of of the pandemic and the entire story of

00:01:02.929 --> 00:01:06.180
opening and school openings and the like.

00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:12.060
And the really crazy thing about the school
starting fiasco is that it's all becoming

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:13.610
laughably political.

00:01:13.610 --> 00:01:16.880
And I want to be careful about saying laughably
because people's lives are at stake here.

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:21.689
But what I mean is it's obviously political
because we're now only talking about a couple

00:01:21.689 --> 00:01:22.899
of months.

00:01:22.899 --> 00:01:27.399
It's just that they are months that are crucial
to Donald Trump's reelection and possibly

00:01:27.399 --> 00:01:32.770
to the reelections of Republicans in the House,
in the Senate gubernatorial Republican reelections.

00:01:32.770 --> 00:01:36.259
And I'll explain what I mean by that and be
really specific.

00:01:36.259 --> 00:01:42.130
You have people on the right like Trump, but
many Republican governors, although Charlie

00:01:42.130 --> 00:01:46.299
Baker here in Massachusetts has been good
on this Republican senators, you have all

00:01:46.299 --> 00:01:51.820
these people saying open the schools now,
open it for economic reasons, open it for

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:52.920
mental health reasons.

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:59.590
You know, being closed leads to suicides and
mental health issues and isolation and all

00:01:59.590 --> 00:02:00.590
of this stuff.

00:02:00.590 --> 00:02:06.560
OK, there gambit is schools being open will
help them get reelected, particularly trump.

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:11.690
The idea being the optics of schools being
open is good politically.

00:02:11.690 --> 00:02:16.690
It'll seem like things are returning to normal
in advance of the November election and there

00:02:16.690 --> 00:02:17.910
is a truth to it.

00:02:17.910 --> 00:02:24.180
I don't deny that there's an economic reality
here where many parents can't work or can't

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:28.120
work as much as they normally would if their
kids are in school because they're essentially

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:30.760
counting on school for childcare.

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:32.040
They are in jobs.

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:35.930
Thanks to our economy that don't pay enough
for them to be able to say, okay, I'll pay

00:02:35.930 --> 00:02:37.849
for childcare and then go to work.

00:02:37.849 --> 00:02:38.959
The numbers don't make sense.

00:02:38.959 --> 00:02:41.180
So I'm completely sensitive to that.

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:43.200
And these are real issues.

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:47.920
I'm not brushing off the issue of opening
schools as something that we shouldn't even

00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:49.900
consider in some places.

00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:55.750
There are counties that have almost no cases,
and in particular, there are these sort of

00:02:55.750 --> 00:03:01.090
semi rural schools where you might have like
seven through twelve, might have 150 kids.

00:03:01.090 --> 00:03:03.489
Right, 25 kids per class.

00:03:03.489 --> 00:03:06.099
You can do that relatively safely.

00:03:06.099 --> 00:03:07.939
And I'm not against doing that.

00:03:07.939 --> 00:03:14.090
The problem is that's not the case in a variety
of places that are opening where we've instantly

00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:18.360
seen cases spread, quarantines start, et cetera.

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:21.470
And again, it's almost September at this point.

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:24.319
We're talking about one semester.

00:03:24.319 --> 00:03:25.510
Had we done.

00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:27.500
It's always too little, too late.

00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:32.890
Had we done a full coordinated shutdown in
the spring, two months, maybe three full mass

00:03:32.890 --> 00:03:37.680
compliance, we would look like many countries,
which now we're doing well and we wouldn't

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:40.260
be having this conversation to the degree
that we are having.

00:03:40.260 --> 00:03:46.180
It would be clear there's a bunch of schools
that can open, but now everything has to stay

00:03:46.180 --> 00:03:47.180
open.

00:03:47.180 --> 00:03:49.159
Things the guidelines are ignored.

00:03:49.159 --> 00:03:50.159
Schools must open.

00:03:50.159 --> 00:03:54.410
And we're in a position where, for political
reasons, Donald Trump and others want to force

00:03:54.410 --> 00:03:55.500
schools open.

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:56.610
And we saw what happened.

00:03:56.610 --> 00:03:57.770
We looked at Georgia.

00:03:57.770 --> 00:03:59.099
We looked at Missouri.

00:03:59.099 --> 00:04:00.860
We're looking at Iowa, Indiana.

00:04:00.860 --> 00:04:04.079
Everywhere, kids and teachers start getting
sick.

00:04:04.079 --> 00:04:06.799
Entire classes have to be quarantined for
weeks.

00:04:06.799 --> 00:04:09.969
You're essentially ending up sending a whole
bunch of people home anyway.

00:04:09.969 --> 00:04:15.280
It would be far more logical, although maybe
not politically beneficial to say let's do

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:16.769
this semester remote.

00:04:16.769 --> 00:04:18.440
We're not saying no school.

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:20.590
We're not saying no school for a long time.

00:04:20.590 --> 00:04:25.610
If things go well, we are hopefully, hopefully
just a couple of months from some vaccine

00:04:25.610 --> 00:04:30.750
approval optimistically, which by the end
of the year, some more significant number

00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:32.890
of people will be able to start getting.

00:04:32.890 --> 00:04:36.680
And in the spring semester, things will start
to normalize with.

00:04:36.680 --> 00:04:38.919
It will still take time.

00:04:38.919 --> 00:04:43.150
But right now, the debate is over just a few
months.

00:04:43.150 --> 00:04:45.300
And what is the real obstacle?

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:46.300
For many parents?

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:47.560
It's the money piece.

00:04:47.560 --> 00:04:53.160
Other countries have said, let's be safe and
let's really send people money and take care

00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:54.160
of people.

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:55.160
The.

00:04:55.160 --> 00:05:01.860
Long run benefit suggests it's warranted in
the U.S. it took months to get one 12 hundred

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:04.200
dollar payment to people.

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:07.720
Who knows if and when the next one is going
to come?

00:05:07.720 --> 00:05:09.560
And that creates this problem.

00:05:09.560 --> 00:05:15.690
It's the same with the desire from many on
the right to cut the unemployment benefits.

00:05:15.690 --> 00:05:20.091
If you do that, you're going to force people
back to work, not safely necessarily, but

00:05:20.091 --> 00:05:22.740
it will create a semblance of normalcy.

00:05:22.740 --> 00:05:27.419
So they will frame it as the left wants everything
closed forever.

00:05:27.419 --> 00:05:31.530
The left wants everything closed until November
4th just to hurt Trump.

00:05:31.530 --> 00:05:32.530
Right.

00:05:32.530 --> 00:05:33.530
One of these two.

00:05:33.530 --> 00:05:34.550
It's almost September.

00:05:34.550 --> 00:05:36.270
We're talking about like three months.

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:38.440
Now, just do school from home.

00:05:38.440 --> 00:05:40.220
We'll get to winter break.

00:05:40.220 --> 00:05:44.940
And then hopefully by then, some portion of
the population will start to be vaccinated.

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:50.050
We'll be starting to get beyond the halfway
point of flu season.

00:05:50.050 --> 00:05:56.780
We're all going to be better off without having
to re shut down because things explode.

00:05:56.780 --> 00:05:57.900
That's disastrous.

00:05:57.900 --> 00:05:59.639
Economically flu season coming.

00:05:59.639 --> 00:06:01.400
I got my flu shot Friday.

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:02.400
Glad to have it.

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:07.419
Dr. Foushee recently said this won't go on
forever, but we have to be safe until we get

00:06:07.419 --> 00:06:08.550
to the other side.

00:06:08.550 --> 00:06:13.600
And now Iowa, which opens schools today with
the first confirmed child corona virus death.

